==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
[[Image:Jetty break2 new(USGS).jpg|thumb|200px||right|Coastal lagoons fronted by barrier spits typically have entrances that migrate through time. Here, the entrance has been fixed by jetty construction. Carlsbad, CA, April 1998.]]
* {{IPA|/ˈdʒɛti/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛti}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|fr}} ''[[jetée]]'' ‘pier, jetty, causeway’. Compare [[jet]], [[jutty]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun|jetties}}

# {{architecture}} A part of a building that jets or projects beyond the rest, and overhangs the wall below.
# A [[wharf]] or [[pier]] extending from the shore.
# ''(Hydraulic engineering):'' A structure of wood or stone extended into the sea to influence the current or tide, or to protect a harbor; a mole; as, the Eads system of jetties at the mouth of the [[Mississippi]] River.

